#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM gratis tentang informasi dan komputasi kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum teleportation"
msgstr "Teleportasi kuantum"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore Biggr */}\n"
"Quantum teleportation, or just teleportation for short, is a protocol where a sender (Alice) transmits a qubit to a receiver (Bob) by making use of a shared entangled quantum state (one e-bit, to be specific) along with two bits of classical communication.\n"
"The name *teleportation* is meant to be suggestive of the concept in science fiction where matter is transported from one location to another by a futuristic process, but it must be understood that matter is not teleported in quantum teleportation — what is actually teleported is quantum information.\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore Biggr */}\n"
"Teleportasi kuantum, atau sekadar teleportasi, adalah protokol di mana pengirim (Alice) mentransmisikan qubit ke penerima (Bob) dengan memanfaatkan keadaan kuantum terjerat yang dibagi (satu e-bit, tepatnya) bersama dengan dua bit komunikasi klasik.\n"
"Nama *teleportasi* dimaksudkan untuk mengingatkan pada konsep dalam fiksi ilmiah di mana materi ditransportasikan dari satu lokasi ke lokasi lain melalui proses futuristik, tetapi harus dipahami bahwa materi tidak diteleportasikan dalam teleportasi kuantum — yang sebenarnya diteleportasikan adalah informasi kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The set-up for teleportation is as follows.\n"
msgstr "Pengaturan untuk teleportasi adalah sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We assume that Alice and Bob share an e-bit: Alice holds a qubit $\\mathsf{A},$ Bob holds a qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ and together the pair $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ is in the state $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"
"It could be, for instance, that Alice and Bob were in the same location in the past, they prepared the qubits $\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B}$ in the state $\\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle,$ and then each went their own way with their qubit in hand.\n"
"Or, it could be that a different process, such as one involving a third party or a complex distributed process, was used to establish this shared e-bit.\n"
"These details are not part of the teleportation protocol itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita mengasumsikan bahwa Alice dan Bob berbagi sebuah e-bit: Alice memegang qubit $\\mathsf{A},$ Bob memegang qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ dan bersama-sama pasangan $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ berada dalam keadaan $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"
"Bisa saja, misalnya, bahwa Alice dan Bob berada di lokasi yang sama di masa lalu, mereka menyiapkan qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ dan $\\mathsf{B}$ dalam keadaan $\\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle,$ dan kemudian masing-masing pergi dengan qubit mereka di tangan.\n"
"Atau, bisa saja proses yang berbeda, seperti yang melibatkan pihak ketiga atau proses terdistribusi yang kompleks, digunakan untuk membangun e-bit yang dibagi ini.\n"
"Detail-detail ini bukan bagian dari protokol teleportasi itu sendiri.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice then comes into possession of a third qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ that she wishes to transmit to Bob.\n"
"The state of the qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ is considered to be *unknown* to Alice and Bob, and no assumptions are made about it.\n"
"For example, the qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ might be entangled with one or more other systems that neither Alice nor Bob can access.\n"
"To say that Alice wishes to transmit the qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ to Bob means that Alice would like Bob to be holding a qubit that is in the same state that $\\mathsf{Q}$ was in at the start of the protocol, having whatever correlations that $\\mathsf{Q}$ had with other systems, as if Alice had physically handed $\\mathsf{Q}$ to Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice kemudian memperoleh qubit ketiga $\\mathsf{Q}$ yang ingin ia transmisikan ke Bob.\n"
"Keadaan qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ dianggap *tidak diketahui* oleh Alice dan Bob, dan tidak ada asumsi yang dibuat tentangnya.\n"
"Misalnya, qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ mungkin terjerat dengan satu atau lebih sistem lain yang tidak dapat diakses oleh Alice maupun Bob.\n"
"Mengatakan bahwa Alice ingin mentransmisikan qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ ke Bob berarti Alice ingin Bob memegang qubit yang berada dalam keadaan yang sama seperti $\\mathsf{Q}$ di awal protokol, memiliki korelasi apa pun yang dimiliki $\\mathsf{Q}$ dengan sistem lain, seolah-olah Alice secara fisik menyerahkan $\\mathsf{Q}$ ke Bob.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We could imagine that Alice physically sends the qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ to Bob, and if it reaches Bob without being altered or disturbed in transit, then Alice and Bob's task will be accomplished.\n"
"In the context of teleportation, however, it is our assumption that this is not feasible; Alice cannot send qubits directly to Bob.\n"
"She may, however, send classical information to Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita bisa membayangkan bahwa Alice secara fisik mengirimkan qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ ke Bob, dan jika sampai ke Bob tanpa diubah atau terganggu dalam perjalanan, maka tugas Alice dan Bob akan terpenuhi.\n"
"Namun dalam konteks teleportasi, asumsi kita adalah bahwa ini tidak layak; Alice tidak bisa mengirim qubit langsung ke Bob.\n"
"Namun ia bisa mengirim informasi klasik ke Bob.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These are reasonable assumptions in a variety of settings.\n"
"For example, if Alice doesn't know Bob's exact location, or the distance between them is large, physically sending a qubit using the technology of today, or the foreseeable future, would be challenging to say the least.\n"
"However, as we know from everyday experiences, classical information transmission under these circumstances is quite straightforward.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah asumsi yang masuk akal dalam berbagai pengaturan.\n"
"Misalnya, jika Alice tidak mengetahui lokasi tepat Bob, atau jarak di antara mereka besar, secara fisik mengirim qubit menggunakan teknologi saat ini, atau masa depan yang dapat dibayangkan, setidaknya akan sangat menantang.\n"
"Namun, seperti yang kita ketahui dari pengalaman sehari-hari, transmisi informasi klasik dalam keadaan seperti ini cukup mudah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point, one might ask whether it is possible for Alice and Bob to accomplish their task without even needing to make use of a shared e-bit.\n"
"In other words, is there any way to transmit a qubit using classical communication alone?\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada titik ini, seseorang mungkin bertanya apakah mungkin bagi Alice dan Bob untuk menyelesaikan tugas mereka tanpa bahkan perlu memanfaatkan e-bit yang dibagi.\n"
"Dengan kata lain, apakah ada cara untuk mentransmisikan qubit menggunakan komunikasi klasik saja?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The answer is no, it is not possible to transmit quantum information using classical communication alone.\n"
"This is not too difficult to prove mathematically using basic quantum information theory, but we can alternatively rule out the possibility of transmitting qubits using classical communication alone by thinking about the no-cloning theorem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jawabannya tidak, tidak mungkin mentransmisikan informasi kuantum menggunakan komunikasi klasik saja.\n"
"Ini tidak terlalu sulit untuk dibuktikan secara matematis menggunakan teori informasi kuantum dasar, tetapi kita juga dapat mengesampingkan kemungkinan mentransmisikan qubit menggunakan komunikasi klasik saja dengan memikirkan teorema no-cloning.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Imagine that there was a way to send quantum information using classical communication alone.\n"
"Classical information can easily be copied and broadcast, which means that any classical transmission from Alice to Bob might also be received by a second receiver (Charlie, let us say).\n"
"But if Charlie receives the same classical communication that Bob received, then would he not also be able to obtain a copy of the qubit $\\mathsf{Q}?$\n"
"This would suggest that $\\mathsf{Q}$ was cloned, which we already know is impossible by the no-cloning theorem, and so we conclude that there is no way to send quantum information using classical communication alone.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bayangkan ada cara untuk mengirim informasi kuantum menggunakan komunikasi klasik saja.\n"
"Informasi klasik dapat dengan mudah disalin dan disiarkan, yang berarti setiap transmisi klasik dari Alice ke Bob juga mungkin diterima oleh penerima kedua (Charlie, katakanlah).\n"
"Tetapi jika Charlie menerima komunikasi klasik yang sama yang diterima Bob, apakah dia tidak juga dapat memperoleh salinan qubit $\\mathsf{Q}?$\n"
"Ini akan menunjukkan bahwa $\\mathsf{Q}$ telah di-kloning, yang sudah kita ketahui tidak mungkin berdasarkan teorema no-cloning, dan sehingga kita menyimpulkan bahwa tidak ada cara untuk mengirim informasi kuantum menggunakan komunikasi klasik saja.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When the assumption that Alice and Bob share an e-bit is in place, however, it is possible for Alice and Bob to accomplish their task.\n"
"This is precisely what the quantum teleportation protocol does.\n"
msgstr ""
"Namun ketika asumsi bahwa Alice dan Bob berbagi e-bit berlaku, Alice dan Bob dapat menyelesaikan tugas mereka.\n"
"Inilah tepatnya yang dilakukan protokol teleportasi kuantum.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Protocol {#protocol}"
msgstr "Protokol {#protocol}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here is a quantum circuit diagram that describes the teleportation "
"protocol:\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah diagram quantum circuit yang menggambarkan protokol "
"teleportasi:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Teleportation circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/teleportation.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Circuit teleportasi](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/teleportation.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The diagram is slightly stylized in that it depicts the separation between Alice and Bob, with two diagonal wires representing classical bits that are sent from Alice to Bob, but otherwise it is an ordinary quantum circuit diagram.\n"
"The qubit names are shown above the wires rather than to the left so that the initial states can be shown as well (which we will commonly do when it is convenient).\n"
"It should also be noted that the $X$ and $Z$ gates have *classical* controls, which simply means that the gates are not applied or applied depending on whether these classical control bits are $0$ or $1,$ respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Diagram ini sedikit distilisasi karena menggambarkan pemisahan antara Alice dan Bob, dengan dua kabel diagonal yang merepresentasikan bit klasik yang dikirim dari Alice ke Bob, tetapi selain itu ini adalah diagram quantum circuit biasa.\n"
"Nama qubit ditampilkan di atas kabel daripada di kiri sehingga keadaan awal juga dapat ditampilkan (yang biasanya kita lakukan bila memudahkan).\n"
"Perlu juga dicatat bahwa gate $X$ dan $Z$ memiliki kontrol *klasik*, yang hanya berarti bahwa gate tidak diterapkan atau diterapkan tergantung pada apakah bit kontrol klasik ini adalah $0$ atau $1,$ masing-masing.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In words, the teleportation protocol is as follows:\n"
msgstr "Dengan kata-kata, protokol teleportasi adalah sebagai berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice performs a controlled-NOT operation on the pair "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{Q}),$ with $\\mathsf{Q}$ being the control and "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ being the target, and then performs a Hadamard operation on "
"$\\mathsf{Q}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice melakukan operasi controlled-NOT pada pasangan "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{Q}),$ dengan $\\mathsf{Q}$ sebagai kontrol dan "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ sebagai target, dan kemudian melakukan operasi Hadamard pada "
"$\\mathsf{Q}.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice then measures both $\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{Q},$ with respect to a "
"standard basis measurement in both cases, and transmits the classical "
"outcomes to Bob. Let us refer to the outcome of the measurement of "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ as $a$ and the outcome of the measurement of $\\mathsf{Q}$ as "
"$b.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice kemudian mengukur $\\mathsf{A}$ dan $\\mathsf{Q},$ dengan pengukuran "
"basis standar di kedua kasus, dan mentransmisikan hasil klasik ke Bob. Sebut"
" hasil pengukuran $\\mathsf{A}$ sebagai $a$ dan hasil pengukuran "
"$\\mathsf{Q}$ sebagai $b.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bob receives $a$ and $b$ from Alice, and depending on the values of these "
"bits he performs these operations:\n"
msgstr ""
"Bob menerima $a$ dan $b$ dari Alice, dan tergantung pada nilai bit-bit ini "
"ia melakukan operasi berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $a = 1,$ then Bob performs a bit flip (or $X$ gate) on his qubit "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika $a = 1,$ maka Bob melakukan bit flip (atau gate $X$) pada qubitnya "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $b = 1,$ then Bob performs a phase flip (or $Z$ gate) on his qubit "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika $b = 1,$ maka Bob melakukan phase flip (atau gate $Z$) pada qubitnya "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   That is, conditioned on $ab$ being $00,$ $01,$ $10,$ or $11,$ Bob "
"performs one of the operations $\\mathbb{I},$ $Z,$ $X,$ or $ZX$ on the qubit"
" $\\mathsf{B}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"   Artinya, dikondisikan pada $ab$ menjadi $00,$ $01,$ $10,$ atau $11,$ Bob "
"melakukan salah satu operasi $\\mathbb{I},$ $Z,$ $X,$ atau $ZX$ pada qubit "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the complete description of the teleportation protocol.\n"
"The analysis that appears below reveals that when it is run, the qubit $\\mathsf{B}$ will be in whatever state $\\mathsf{Q}$ was in prior to the protocol being executed, including whatever correlations it had with any other systems — which is to say that the protocol has effectively implemented a perfect qubit communication channel, where the state of $\\mathsf{Q}$ has been \"teleported\" into $\\mathsf{B}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Inilah deskripsi lengkap dari protokol teleportasi.\n"
"Analisis yang muncul di bawah mengungkapkan bahwa ketika dijalankan, qubit $\\mathsf{B}$ akan berada dalam keadaan apa pun yang dimiliki $\\mathsf{Q}$ sebelum protokol dijalankan, termasuk korelasi apa pun yang dimilikinya dengan sistem lain — yang berarti bahwa protokol telah secara efektif mengimplementasikan channel komunikasi qubit yang sempurna, di mana keadaan $\\mathsf{Q}$ telah \"diteleportasikan\" ke $\\mathsf{B}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before proceeding to the analysis, notice that this protocol does not succeed in cloning the state of $\\mathsf{Q},$ which we already know is impossible by the no-cloning theorem.\n"
"Rather, when the protocol is finished, the state of the qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ will have changed from its original value to $\\vert b\\rangle$ as a result of the measurement performed on it.\n"
"Also notice that the e-bit has effectively been \"burned\" in the process: the state of $\\mathsf{A}$ has changed to $\\vert a\\rangle$ and is no longer entangled with $\\mathsf{B}$ (or any other system).\n"
"This is the cost of teleportation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebelum melanjutkan ke analisis, perhatikan bahwa protokol ini tidak berhasil mengkloning keadaan $\\mathsf{Q},$ yang sudah kita ketahui tidak mungkin berdasarkan teorema no-cloning.\n"
"Sebaliknya, ketika protokol selesai, keadaan qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ akan telah berubah dari nilai aslinya menjadi $\\vert b\\rangle$ sebagai akibat dari pengukuran yang dilakukan padanya.\n"
"Perhatikan juga bahwa e-bit telah secara efektif \"terbakar\" dalam prosesnya: keadaan $\\mathsf{A}$ telah berubah menjadi $\\vert a\\rangle$ dan tidak lagi terjerat dengan $\\mathsf{B}$ (atau sistem lainnya).\n"
"Inilah biaya teleportasi.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Analysis {#analysis}"
msgstr "Analisis {#analysis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To analyze the teleportation protocol, we'll examine the behavior of the circuit described above, one step at a time, beginning with the situation in which $\\mathsf{Q}$ is initially in the state $\\alpha\\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"This is not the most general situation, as it does not capture the possibility that $\\mathsf{Q}$ is entangled with other systems, but starting with this simpler case will add clarity to the analysis.\n"
"The more general case is addressed below, following the analysis of the simpler case.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menganalisis protokol teleportasi, kita akan memeriksa perilaku circuit yang dijelaskan di atas, satu langkah setiap saat, dimulai dengan situasi di mana $\\mathsf{Q}$ awalnya dalam keadaan $\\alpha\\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"Ini bukan situasi yang paling umum, karena tidak menangkap kemungkinan bahwa $\\mathsf{Q}$ terjerat dengan sistem lain, tetapi memulai dengan kasus yang lebih sederhana ini akan menambah kejelasan pada analisis.\n"
"Kasus yang lebih umum dibahas di bawah ini, mengikuti analisis dari kasus yang lebih sederhana.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Specifically, we will consider the states of the qubits "
"$(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{Q})$ at the times suggested by this "
"figure:\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara khusus, kita akan mempertimbangkan keadaan qubit "
"$(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{Q})$ pada waktu yang disarankan oleh "
"gambar ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Teleportation circuit time-steps](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/teleportation-time-steps.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Langkah waktu circuit teleportasi](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/teleportation-time-steps.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Under the assumption that the qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ begins the protocol in the"
" state $\\alpha\\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle,$ the state of the "
"three qubits $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{Q})$ together at the start "
"of the protocol is therefore\n"
msgstr ""
"Di bawah asumsi bahwa qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ memulai protokol dalam keadaan "
"$\\alpha\\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle,$ keadaan tiga qubit "
"$(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{Q})$ bersama-sama di awal protokol "
"karenanya adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_0 \\rangle\n"
"= \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\otimes\n"
"\\bigl(\\alpha\\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"= \\frac{\\alpha \\vert 000 \\rangle + \\alpha \\vert 110\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 001\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 111\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_0 \\rangle\n"
"= \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\otimes\n"
"\\bigl(\\alpha\\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"= \\frac{\\alpha \\vert 000 \\rangle + \\alpha \\vert 110\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 001\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 111\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first gate that is performed is the controlled-NOT gate, which "
"transforms the state $\\vert\\pi_0\\rangle$ into\n"
msgstr ""
"Gate pertama yang dilakukan adalah gate controlled-NOT, yang mengubah "
"keadaan $\\vert\\pi_0\\rangle$ menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_1 \\rangle  = \\frac{\\alpha \\vert 000 \\rangle + \\alpha \\vert 110\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 011\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 101\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_1 \\rangle  = \\frac{\\alpha \\vert 000 \\rangle + \\alpha \\vert 110\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 011\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 101\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then the Hadamard gate is applied, which transforms the state "
"$\\vert\\pi_1\\rangle$ into\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian gate Hadamard diterapkan, yang mengubah keadaan "
"$\\vert\\pi_1\\rangle$ menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle\n"
"& =\n"
"\\frac{\\alpha \\vert 00\\rangle \\vert + \\rangle + \\alpha \\vert 11\\rangle\\vert +\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 01\\rangle\\vert -\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 10\\rangle\\vert -\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\frac{\\alpha \\vert 000 \\rangle\n"
"+ \\alpha \\vert 001 \\rangle\n"
"+ \\alpha \\vert 110 \\rangle\n"
"+ \\alpha \\vert 111 \\rangle\n"
"+ \\beta \\vert 010 \\rangle\n"
"- \\beta \\vert 011 \\rangle\n"
"+ \\beta \\vert 100 \\rangle\n"
"- \\beta \\vert 101 \\rangle}{2}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle\n"
"& =\n"
"\\frac{\\alpha \\vert 00\\rangle \\vert + \\rangle + \\alpha \\vert 11\\rangle\\vert +\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 01\\rangle\\vert -\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 10\\rangle\\vert -\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\frac{\\alpha \\vert 000 \\rangle\n"
"+ \\alpha \\vert 001 \\rangle\n"
"+ \\alpha \\vert 110 \\rangle\n"
"+ \\alpha \\vert 111 \\rangle\n"
"+ \\beta \\vert 010 \\rangle\n"
"- \\beta \\vert 011 \\rangle\n"
"+ \\beta \\vert 100 \\rangle\n"
"- \\beta \\vert 101 \\rangle}{2}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using the multilinearity of the tensor product, we may alternatively write "
"this state as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan multilinearitas dari produk tensor, kita dapat menulis keadaan "
"ini secara alternatif sebagai berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle = \\quad\n"
"& \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl(\\alpha\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\vert 00\\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"+ & \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl(\\alpha\\vert 0 \\rangle - \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\vert 01\\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"+ & \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl(\\alpha\\vert 1 \\rangle + \\beta \\vert 0\\rangle \\bigr)\\vert 10\\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"+ & \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl(\\alpha\\vert 1 \\rangle - \\beta \\vert 0\\rangle \\bigr)\\vert 11\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle = \\quad\n"
"& \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl(\\alpha\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\vert 00\\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"+ & \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl(\\alpha\\vert 0 \\rangle - \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\vert 01\\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"+ & \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl(\\alpha\\vert 1 \\rangle + \\beta \\vert 0\\rangle \\bigr)\\vert 10\\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"+ & \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl(\\alpha\\vert 1 \\rangle - \\beta \\vert 0\\rangle \\bigr)\\vert 11\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At first glance, it might look like something magical has happened, because the leftmost qubit $\\mathsf{B}$ now seems to depend on the numbers $\\alpha$ and $\\beta,$ even though there has not yet been any communication from Alice to Bob.\n"
"This is an illusion.\n"
"Scalars float freely through tensor products, so $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are neither more nor less associated with the leftmost qubit than they are with the other qubits, and all we have done is to use algebra to express the state in a way that facilitates an analysis of the measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada pandangan pertama, mungkin terlihat seperti sesuatu yang ajaib telah terjadi, karena qubit paling kiri $\\mathsf{B}$ sekarang tampaknya bergantung pada angka $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta,$ meskipun belum ada komunikasi dari Alice ke Bob.\n"
"Ini adalah ilusi.\n"
"Skalar mengalir bebas melalui produk tensor, sehingga $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$ tidak lebih atau kurang terkait dengan qubit paling kiri daripada dengan qubit lainnya, dan yang telah kita lakukan hanyalah menggunakan aljabar untuk mengekspresikan keadaan dengan cara yang memfasilitasi analisis pengukuran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let us consider the four possible outcomes of Alice's standard basis "
"measurements, together with the actions that Bob performs as a result.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang mari kita pertimbangkan empat kemungkinan hasil dari pengukuran "
"basis standar Alice, bersama dengan tindakan yang dilakukan Bob sebagai "
"hasilnya.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Possible outcomes {#possible-outcomes}"
msgstr "Kemungkinan hasil {#possible-outcomes}"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The outcome of Alice's measurement is $aq = 00$ with probability\n"
msgstr "Hasil pengukuran Alice adalah $aq = 00$ dengan probabilitas\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\Biggl\\| \\frac{1}{2}\\bigl(\\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle\\bigr) \\Biggr\\|^2\n"
"   = \\frac{\\vert\\alpha\\vert^2 + \\vert\\beta\\vert^2}{4} = \\frac{1}{4},\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\Biggl\\| \\frac{1}{2}\\bigl(\\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle\\bigr) \\Biggr\\|^2\n"
"   = \\frac{\\vert\\alpha\\vert^2 + \\vert\\beta\\vert^2}{4} = \\frac{1}{4},\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   in which case the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{Q})$ "
"becomes\n"
msgstr "   dalam hal ini keadaan $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{Q})$ menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl( \\alpha \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 00 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl( \\alpha \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 00 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Bob does nothing in this case, and so this is the final state of these "
"three qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Bob tidak melakukan apa pun dalam kasus ini, sehingga inilah keadaan "
"akhir dari tiga qubit ini.\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The outcome of Alice's measurement is $aq = 01$ with probability\n"
msgstr "Hasil pengukuran Alice adalah $aq = 01$ dengan probabilitas\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\Biggl\\| \\frac{1}{2}\\bigl(\\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle - \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle\\bigr) \\Biggr\\|^2\n"
"   = \\frac{\\vert\\alpha\\vert^2 + \\vert{-\\beta}\\vert^2}{4} = \\frac{1}{4},\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\Biggl\\| \\frac{1}{2}\\bigl(\\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle - \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle\\bigr) \\Biggr\\|^2\n"
"   = \\frac{\\vert\\alpha\\vert^2 + \\vert{-\\beta}\\vert^2}{4} = \\frac{1}{4},\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl( \\alpha \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\beta \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 01 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl( \\alpha \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\beta \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 01 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In this case Bob applies a $Z$ gate to $\\mathsf{B},$ leaving "
"$(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{Q})$ in the state\n"
msgstr ""
"   Dalam kasus ini Bob menerapkan gate $Z$ pada $\\mathsf{B},$ meninggalkan "
"$(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{Q})$ dalam keadaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl( \\alpha \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 01 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl( \\alpha \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 01 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The outcome of Alice's measurement is $aq = 10$ with probability\n"
msgstr "Hasil pengukuran Alice adalah $aq = 10$ dengan probabilitas\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\Biggl\\| \\frac{1}{2}\\bigl(\\alpha \\vert 1\\rangle + \\beta\\vert 0\\rangle\\bigr) \\Biggr\\|^2\n"
"   = \\frac{\\vert\\alpha\\vert^2 + \\vert\\beta\\vert^2}{4} = \\frac{1}{4},\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\Biggl\\| \\frac{1}{2}\\bigl(\\alpha \\vert 1\\rangle + \\beta\\vert 0\\rangle\\bigr) \\Biggr\\|^2\n"
"   = \\frac{\\vert\\alpha\\vert^2 + \\vert\\beta\\vert^2}{4} = \\frac{1}{4},\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl( \\alpha \\vert 1 \\rangle + \\beta \\vert 0 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 10 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl( \\alpha \\vert 1 \\rangle + \\beta \\vert 0 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 10 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In this case, Bob applies an $X$ gate to the qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ leaving"
" $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{Q})$ in the state\n"
msgstr ""
"   Dalam kasus ini, Bob menerapkan gate $X$ pada qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ "
"meninggalkan $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{Q})$ dalam keadaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl( \\alpha \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 10 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl( \\alpha \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 10 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The outcome of Alice's measurement is $aq = 11$ with probability\n"
msgstr "Hasil pengukuran Alice adalah $aq = 11$ dengan probabilitas\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\Biggl\\| \\frac{1}{2}\\bigl(\\alpha \\vert 1\\rangle - \\beta\\vert 0\\rangle\\bigr) \\Biggr\\|^2\n"
"   = \\frac{\\vert\\alpha\\vert^2 + \\vert{-\\beta}\\vert^2}{4} = \\frac{1}{4},\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\Biggl\\| \\frac{1}{2}\\bigl(\\alpha \\vert 1\\rangle - \\beta\\vert 0\\rangle\\bigr) \\Biggr\\|^2\n"
"   = \\frac{\\vert\\alpha\\vert^2 + \\vert{-\\beta}\\vert^2}{4} = \\frac{1}{4},\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl( \\alpha \\vert 1 \\rangle - \\beta \\vert 0 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 11 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl( \\alpha \\vert 1 \\rangle - \\beta \\vert 0 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 11 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In this case, Bob performs the operation $ZX$ on the qubit $\\mathsf{B},$"
" leaving $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{Q})$ in the state\n"
msgstr ""
"   Dalam kasus ini, Bob melakukan operasi $ZX$ pada qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ "
"meninggalkan $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{Q})$ dalam keadaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl( \\alpha \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 11 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl( \\alpha \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 11 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now see, in all four cases, that Bob's qubit $\\mathsf{B}$ is left in the state\n"
"$\\alpha\\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle$ at the end of the protocol, which is the initial state of the qubit $\\mathsf{Q}.$\n"
"This is what we wanted to show: the teleportation protocol has worked correctly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita melihat, dalam keempat kasus, bahwa qubit Bob $\\mathsf{B}$ ditinggalkan dalam keadaan\n"
"$\\alpha\\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle$ di akhir protokol, yang merupakan keadaan awal qubit $\\mathsf{Q}.$\n"
"Inilah yang ingin kita tunjukkan: protokol teleportasi telah bekerja dengan benar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We also see that the qubits $\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{Q}$ are left in one of the four states $\\vert 00\\rangle,$ $\\vert 01\\rangle,$ $\\vert 10\\rangle,$ or $\\vert 11\\rangle,$ each with probability $1/4,$ depending upon the measurement outcomes that Alice obtained.\n"
"Thus, as was already suggested above, at the end of the protocol Alice no longer has the state $\\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle,$ which is consistent with the no-cloning theorem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita juga melihat bahwa qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ dan $\\mathsf{Q}$ ditinggalkan dalam salah satu dari empat keadaan $\\vert 00\\rangle,$ $\\vert 01\\rangle,$ $\\vert 10\\rangle,$ atau $\\vert 11\\rangle,$ masing-masing dengan probabilitas $1/4,$ tergantung pada hasil pengukuran yang diperoleh Alice.\n"
"Jadi, seperti yang telah disarankan di atas, di akhir protokol Alice tidak lagi memiliki keadaan $\\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle,$ yang konsisten dengan teorema no-cloning.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that Alice's measurements yield absolutely no information about the state $\\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"That is, the probability for each of the four possible measurement outcomes is $1/4,$ irrespective of $\\alpha$ and $\\beta.$\n"
"This is also essential for teleportation to work correctly.\n"
"Extracting information from an unknown quantum state necessarily disturbs it in general, but here Bob obtains the state without it being disturbed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa pengukuran Alice sama sekali tidak memberikan informasi tentang keadaan $\\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"Artinya, probabilitas untuk setiap empat kemungkinan hasil pengukuran adalah $1/4,$ terlepas dari $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta.$\n"
"Ini juga penting agar teleportasi bekerja dengan benar.\n"
"Mengekstraksi informasi dari keadaan kuantum yang tidak diketahui pasti mengganggunya secara umum, tetapi di sini Bob memperoleh keadaan tanpa terganggu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's consider the more general situation in which the qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ is initially entangled with another system, which we'll name $\\mathsf{R}.$\n"
"A similar analysis to the one above reveals that the teleportation protocol functions correctly in this more general case:\n"
"at the end of the protocol, the qubit $\\mathsf{B}$ held by Bob is entangled with $\\mathsf{R}$ in the same way that $\\mathsf{Q}$ was at the start of the protocol, as if Alice had simply handed $\\mathsf{Q}$ to Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang mari kita pertimbangkan situasi yang lebih umum di mana qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ awalnya terjerat dengan sistem lain, yang akan kita beri nama $\\mathsf{R}.$\n"
"Analisis serupa dengan yang di atas mengungkapkan bahwa protokol teleportasi berfungsi dengan benar dalam kasus yang lebih umum ini:\n"
"di akhir protokol, qubit $\\mathsf{B}$ yang dipegang Bob terjerat dengan $\\mathsf{R}$ dengan cara yang sama seperti $\\mathsf{Q}$ di awal protokol, seolah-olah Alice telah menyerahkan $\\mathsf{Q}$ ke Bob.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To prove this, let us suppose that the state of the pair "
"$(\\mathsf{Q},\\mathsf{R})$ is initially given by a quantum state vector of "
"the form\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk membuktikan ini, misalkan keadaan pasangan $(\\mathsf{Q},\\mathsf{R})$"
" awalnya diberikan oleh vektor keadaan kuantum dalam bentuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha \\vert 0 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{Q}} \\vert \\gamma_0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"+ \\beta \\vert 1 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{Q}} \\vert \\gamma_1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha \\vert 0 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{Q}} \\vert \\gamma_0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"+ \\beta \\vert 1 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{Q}} \\vert \\gamma_1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle$ are quantum state vectors for the system $\\mathsf{R}$ and $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are complex numbers satisfying $\\vert \\alpha \\vert^2 + \\vert\\beta\\vert^2 = 1.$\n"
"Any quantum state vector of the pair $(\\mathsf{Q},\\mathsf{R})$ can be expressed in this way.\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle$ dan $\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle$ adalah vektor keadaan kuantum untuk sistem $\\mathsf{R}$ dan $\\alpha$ serta $\\beta$ adalah bilangan kompleks yang memenuhi $\\vert \\alpha \\vert^2 + \\vert\\beta\\vert^2 = 1.$\n"
"Setiap vektor keadaan kuantum dari pasangan $(\\mathsf{Q},\\mathsf{R})$ dapat diekspresikan dengan cara ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following figure depicts the same circuit as before, with the addition "
"of the system $\\mathsf{R}$ (represented by a collection of qubits on the "
"top of the diagram that nothing happens to).\n"
msgstr ""
"Gambar berikut menggambarkan circuit yang sama seperti sebelumnya, dengan "
"penambahan sistem $\\mathsf{R}$ (direpresentasikan oleh kumpulan qubit di "
"bagian atas diagram yang tidak ada yang terjadi padanya).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Teleportation with an entangled input](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/teleportation-with-"
"entanglement.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Teleportasi dengan masukan terjerat](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/teleportation-with-"
"entanglement.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To analyze what happens when the teleportation protocol is run, it is helpful to permute the systems, along the same lines that was described in the previous lesson.\n"
"Specifically, we'll consider the state of the systems in the order $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{R},\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{Q})$ rather than $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{Q},\\mathsf{R}).$\n"
"The names of the various systems are included as subscripts in the expressions that follow for clarity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menganalisis apa yang terjadi ketika protokol teleportasi dijalankan, akan sangat membantu untuk mempermutasi (menukar urutan) sistem, mengikuti garis yang sama seperti yang dijelaskan dalam pelajaran sebelumnya.\n"
"Secara khusus, kita akan mempertimbangkan keadaan sistem dalam urutan $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{R},\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{Q})$ daripada $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{Q},\\mathsf{R}).$\n"
"Nama berbagai sistem disertakan sebagai subskrip dalam ekspresi yang mengikuti untuk kejelasan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At the start of the protocol, the state of these systems is as follows:\n"
msgstr "Di awal protokol, keadaan sistem-sistem ini adalah sebagai berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert \\pi_0\\rangle\n"
"& = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle_{\\mathsf{BA}} \\otimes \\bigl(\n"
"  \\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Q}} \\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"+ \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Q}}\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\\bigr)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\frac{\n"
"  \\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert \\gamma_0 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}} \\vert 00 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}\n"
"+ \\alpha \\vert 1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert \\gamma_0 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}} \\vert 10 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}\n"
"+ \\beta \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert \\gamma_1 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}} \\vert 01 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}\n"
"+ \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert \\gamma_1 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}} \\vert 11 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert \\pi_0\\rangle\n"
"& = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle_{\\mathsf{BA}} \\otimes \\bigl(\n"
"  \\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Q}} \\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"+ \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Q}}\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\\bigr)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\frac{\n"
"  \\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert \\gamma_0 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}} \\vert 00 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}\n"
"+ \\alpha \\vert 1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert \\gamma_0 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}} \\vert 10 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}\n"
"+ \\beta \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert \\gamma_1 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}} \\vert 01 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}\n"
"+ \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert \\gamma_1 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}} \\vert 11 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First the controlled-NOT gate is applied, which transforms this state to\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama gate controlled-NOT diterapkan, yang mengubah keadaan ini menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\pi_1\\rangle =\n"
"\\frac{\n"
"  \\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_0 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}} \\vert 00\\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}\n"
"+ \\alpha \\vert 1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_0 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}} \\vert 10\\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}\n"
"+ \\beta \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_1 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}} \\vert 11\\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}\n"
"+ \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_1 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}} \\vert 01\\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\pi_1\\rangle =\n"
"\\frac{\n"
"  \\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_0 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}} \\vert 00\\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}\n"
"+ \\alpha \\vert 1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_0 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}} \\vert 10\\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}\n"
"+ \\beta \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_1 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}} \\vert 11\\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}\n"
"+ \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_1 \\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}} \\vert 01\\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then the Hadamard gate is applied.\n"
"After expanding and simplifying the resulting state, along similar lines to the analysis of the simpler case above, we obtain this expression of the resulting state:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian gate Hadamard diterapkan.\n"
"Setelah memperluas dan menyederhanakan keadaan yang dihasilkan, mengikuti garis yang sama seperti analisis kasus yang lebih sederhana di atas, kita mendapatkan ekspresi dari keadaan yang dihasilkan ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert \\pi_2 \\rangle = \\quad\n"
"  & \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl(\n"
"   \\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"  + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"  \\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  + & \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl(\n"
"   \\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"  - \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"  \\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  + & \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl(\n"
"   \\alpha \\vert 1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"  + \\beta \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"  \\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  + & \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl(\n"
"   \\alpha \\vert 1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"  - \\beta \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"  \\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert \\pi_2 \\rangle = \\quad\n"
"  & \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl(\n"
"   \\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"  + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"  \\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  + & \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl(\n"
"   \\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"  - \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"  \\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  + & \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl(\n"
"   \\alpha \\vert 1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"  + \\beta \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"  \\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  + & \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl(\n"
"   \\alpha \\vert 1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"  - \\beta \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{B}} \\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle_{\\mathsf{R}}\n"
"  \\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle_{\\mathsf{AQ}}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Proceeding exactly as before, where we consider the four different possible "
"outcomes of Alice's measurements along with the corresponding actions "
"performed by Bob, we find that at the end of the protocol, the state of "
"$(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{R})$ is always\n"
msgstr ""
"Melanjutkan persis seperti sebelumnya, di mana kita mempertimbangkan empat "
"kemungkinan hasil pengukuran Alice bersama dengan tindakan yang bersesuaian "
"yang dilakukan Bob, kita menemukan bahwa di akhir protokol, keadaan "
"$(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{R})$ selalu\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert \\gamma_0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert \\gamma_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha \\vert 0 \\rangle \\vert \\gamma_0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1 \\rangle \\vert \\gamma_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Informally speaking, the analysis does not change in a significant way as compared with the simpler case above;\n"
"$\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle$ essentially just \"come along for the ride.\"\n"
"So, teleportation succeeds in creating a perfect quantum communication channel, effectively transmitting the contents of the qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ into $\\mathsf{B}$ and preserving all correlations with other systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara informal, analisisnya tidak berubah secara signifikan dibandingkan dengan kasus yang lebih sederhana di atas;\n"
"$\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle$ dan $\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle$ pada dasarnya hanya \"ikut serta dalam perjalanan.\"\n"
"Jadi, teleportasi berhasil menciptakan channel komunikasi kuantum yang sempurna, secara efektif mentransmisikan isi qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ ke $\\mathsf{B}$ dan melestarikan semua korelasi dengan sistem lain.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is actually not surprising at all, given the analysis of the simpler case above.\n"
"As that analysis revealed, we have a physical process that acts like the identity operation on a qubit in an arbitrary quantum state, and there's only one way that can happen: the operation implemented by the protocol must *be* the identity operation.\n"
"That is, once we know that teleportation works correctly for a single qubit in isolation, we can conclude that the protocol effectively implements a perfect, noiseless quantum channel, and so it must work correctly even if the input qubit is entangled with another system.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini sebenarnya tidak mengejutkan sama sekali, mengingat analisis kasus yang lebih sederhana di atas.\n"
"Seperti yang diungkapkan analisis tersebut, kita memiliki proses fisik yang bertindak seperti operasi identitas pada qubit dalam keadaan kuantum sembarang, dan hanya ada satu cara itu bisa terjadi: operasi yang diimplementasikan oleh protokol harus *menjadi* operasi identitas.\n"
"Artinya, begitu kita mengetahui bahwa teleportasi bekerja dengan benar untuk qubit tunggal yang terisolasi, kita dapat menyimpulkan bahwa protokol secara efektif mengimplementasikan channel kuantum yang sempurna dan tanpa derau, sehingga harus bekerja dengan benar meskipun qubit masukan terjerat dengan sistem lain.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Further discussion {#further-discussion}"
msgstr "Diskusi lebih lanjut {#further-discussion}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here are a few brief, concluding remarks on teleportation.\n"
msgstr "Berikut adalah beberapa catatan singkat penutup tentang teleportasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, teleportation is not an *application* of quantum information, it's a *protocol* for performing quantum communication.\n"
"It is therefore useful only insofar as quantum communication is useful.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, teleportasi bukan *aplikasi* informasi kuantum, melainkan *protokol* untuk melakukan komunikasi kuantum.\n"
"Oleh karena itu berguna hanya sejauh komunikasi kuantum berguna.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Indeed, it is reasonable to speculate that teleportation could one day become a standard way to communicate quantum information, perhaps through a process known as *entanglement distillation*.\n"
"This is a process that converts a larger number of noisy (or imperfect) e-bits into a smaller number of high quality e-bits, that could then be used for noiseless or near-noiseless teleportation.\n"
"The idea is that the process of entanglement distillation is not as delicate as direct quantum communication.\n"
"We could accept losses, for instance, and if the process doesn't work out, we can just try again.\n"
"In contrast, the actual qubits we hope to communicate might be much more precious.\n"
msgstr ""
"Memang, masuk akal untuk berspekulasi bahwa teleportasi suatu hari bisa menjadi cara standar untuk mengkomunikasikan informasi kuantum, mungkin melalui proses yang dikenal sebagai *distilasi keterikatan*.\n"
"Ini adalah proses yang mengubah sejumlah besar e-bit yang berderau (atau tidak sempurna) menjadi sejumlah kecil e-bit berkualitas tinggi, yang kemudian dapat digunakan untuk teleportasi tanpa derau atau mendekati tanpa derau.\n"
"Idenya adalah bahwa proses distilasi keterikatan tidak selembut komunikasi kuantum langsung.\n"
"Kita bisa menerima kerugian, misalnya, dan jika prosesnya tidak berhasil, kita bisa mencoba lagi.\n"
"Sebaliknya, qubit aktual yang ingin kita komunikasikan mungkin jauh lebih berharga.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, it should be understood that the idea behind teleportation and the way that it works is quite fundamental in quantum information and computation.\n"
"It really is a cornerstone of quantum information theory, and variations of it arise.\n"
"For example, quantum gates can be implemented through a closely related process known as *quantum gate teleportation*, which uses teleportation to apply *operations* to qubits rather than communicating them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, harus dipahami bahwa ide di balik teleportasi dan cara kerjanya sangat fundamental dalam informasi dan komputasi kuantum.\n"
"Ini benar-benar merupakan landasan teori informasi kuantum, dan variasinya muncul.\n"
"Misalnya, gate kuantum dapat diimplementasikan melalui proses yang erat kaitannya dikenal sebagai *teleportasi gate kuantum*, yang menggunakan teleportasi untuk menerapkan *operasi* pada qubit daripada mengkomunikasikannya.\n"
